===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰreh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|brawne}}, from {{der|en|fro|braon||slice of meat, fleshy part, buttock}}, from {{der|en|frk|*brādon}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*brādan}}, accusative form of {{m|gmw-pro|*brādō||roasted meat, ham}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*brēdô||meat, roast}}, of uncertain further origin, but possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰreh₁-||to burn, heat}}.

Akin to {{cog|goh|brāto||tender meat}} ({{cog|de|Braten||roast}}), {{cog|ang|brǣde}}, {{m|ang|brǣd|t=flesh, meat}}, {{cog|non|bráð||raw meat}}.

