===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Strong [[muscle]]s or [[lean]] [[flesh]], especially of the arm, leg or thumb.
# Physical [[strength]]; [[muscularity]].
#: {{ux|en|The builders at the site had more '''brawn''' than brain.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Stephanie Laurens|title=A Secret Love|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=UIA1KBh1iLAC&pg=PA349|page=349|publisher=Avon Books|year_published=2000|isbn=0380805707
|passage=The man was a bruiser, the sort who'd learned his science in tavern brawls. Given his size and lack of agility, he relied on his '''brawn''' to win. In any wrestling match, Crowley would triumph easily.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Michael Mandaville|title=Stealing Thunder|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=U-xdpBsgoGUC&pg=PA562|page=562|publisher=Dog Ear Publishing|year_published=2008|isbn=9781598585353
|passage=The two men were husky, picked for their '''brawn''' by the little man who sauntered into the room.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Martin Pasko; Robert Greenberger|title=The Essential Superman Encyclopedia|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=aknpy8JiMWEC&pg=PA218|page=218|publisher=Del Ray|year_published=2010|isbn=9780345501080
|passage=The youth agreed to the scheme and used his '''brawn''' to begin moving pieces into place, starting by moving the planet Rann into the Thanagarian star system {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|British}} [[head cheese|Head cheese]]; a [[terrine]] made from the [[head]] of a [[pig]] or [[calf]]; originally [[boar]]'s meat.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1820|author=w:Percy Bysshe Shelley|title=Oedipus Tyrannus; Or, Swellfoot The Tyrant: A Tragedy in Two Acts
|passage=Now if your Majesty would have our bristles<br>To bind your mortar with, or fill our colons<br>With rich blood, or make '''brawn''' out of our gristles,<br>In policy—ask else your royal Solons—<br>You ought to give us hog-wash and clean straw,<br>And sties well thatched; besides it is the law!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|author=w:Jane Gardam|title=God on the Rocks|publisher=Abacus|year_published=2014|page=111
|passage=It was '''brawn''' and shape for high tea.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|dialectal}} A [[boar]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1821|author=John Stagg|title=The Cumbrian Minstrel: Being a Poetical Miscellany
|passage=And loud as '''brawns''' wer [they] snoring,}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1842|author=Moses Aaron Richardson|title=The Borderer's Table Book: Or, Gatherings of the Local History
|passage=THE village of Brancepath, pleasantly situated at the distance of four miles and three- quarters south-west by west of Durham, is said to have derived its name (a corruption of Brawn's-path) from a '''brawn''' of vast size, [...]}}

